WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:16.690
House of the Dragon, a Game of Thrones prequel
show, is coming in 2022 on HBO

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:19.580
and Targaryen dragons are coming with it.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.110
It will feature around 20 dragons and in the
part 1 I covered many of them.

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:28.010
We start part 2 with the most beautiful Targaryen
dragon, Sunfyre.

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:33.250
Sunfyre, known as Sunfyre the Golden, was
the mount of Aegon II Targaryen during the

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:34.399
Dance of the Dragons.

00:00:34.399 --> 00:00:39.000
He is one of the dragons HBO shared in their
announcment few days ago.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.700
According to some sources, Sunfyre was the
most beautiful dragon ever seen upon the earth.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:49.510
Sunfyre had gleaming gold scales and his flames
were golden as well.

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:55.100
During the siege of Rook's Rest, Rhaenys Targaryen
arrived riding the large older red dragon

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.510
Meleys
to attempt to lift the siege of the castle.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:03.190
This was all a trap, however, as the Greens
had kept two of their own dragons hidden and

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:07.610
in reserve so they could take Meleys in an
uneven fight.

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:13.450
Aegon II appeared riding the younger but strong
Sunfyre, and his younger brother Aemond Targaryen

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:19.450
also attacked riding the massive Vhagar, last
of the first generation Targaryen dragons.

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:24.920
Rhaenys could not prevail against such odds,
yet she did not flee but flew head-on to meet

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:26.249
her attackers.

00:01:26.249 --> 00:01:30.960
Meleys was still so large and powerful that
she put up a brutal fight.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:36.219
When the dust settled Meleys was dead and
Vhagar was relatively unharmed, but Sunfyre

00:01:36.219 --> 00:01:39.289
had been nearly killed and permanently maimed.

00:01:39.289 --> 00:01:44.609
Meleys managed to nearly rip one of his wing-arms
completely from his body, and as for Aegon

00:01:44.609 --> 00:01:49.840
II, he was left horrifically burned and with
multiple broken bones.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:54.179
Sunfyre survived the battle but the world's
most beautiful living dragon was left crippled

00:01:54.179 --> 00:01:58.170
and heavily scarred, just like its rider,
Aegon.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.520
Aegon and Sunfyre reunited at Dragonstone.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:05.869
When Sunfyre arrived he fought and killed
a remaining riderless dragon, Grey Ghost - though

00:02:05.869 --> 00:02:08.149
he took yet more wounds in the process.

00:02:08.149 --> 00:02:14.000
When Aegon finally rode Sunfyre again, he
was attacked by Daemon's young daughter Baela

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:19.470
riding the dragon Moondancer - an even younger
dragon barely large enough to carry the 13

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:20.770
year old girl.

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:25.860
Moondancer was quick, however, while Sunfyre
was still half-crippled and slowed by his

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:26.860
injuries.

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:30.550
They were therefore evenly matched and their
duel was ferocious.

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:36.600
It culminated when Sunfyre tackled Moondancer
in mid-air and drove her into the ground below:

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:40.670
his larger size meant that he survived the
fall while she was killed.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:45.670
Nonetheless Sunfyre was mortally injured by
this fight, and would never fly again.

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:47.840
Sunfye died soon after.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:52.640
Despite being one of the younger dragons in
the Dance, Sunfyre actually shared the highest

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:58.090
dragon versus dragon kill count with the massive
Vhagar herself: two individual kills and one

00:02:58.090 --> 00:02:59.480
assisted.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:03.920
Both Sunfyre and Vhagar died as a result of
their third dragon fights.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:07.880
For that matter, they were the only two dragons
in the Dance who ever lived through a dragon

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:12.970
versus dragon fight and lived (most dragons
in the war were actually killed by human armies,

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:17.430
or died in mutual kills in their first battle
against another dragon).

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:23.710
Next we have Stormcloud who was a young male
dragon bonded with King Aegon III Targaryen.

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:26.910
Aegon used Stormloud to escape an ambush at
the sea.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:32.920
Prince Aegon managed to reach Dragonstone,
clinging desperately to his dragon's neck.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:37.120
Stormcloud had been terribly wounded as he
fled; when he arrived at Dragonstone stubs

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:41.680
of countless arrows were embedded in his belly,
and there was a scorpion bolt through his

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.120
neck.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:48.010
Stormcloud died within an hour, hissing as
the hot blood gushed black and smoke from

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:49.410
his wounds.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:52.910
After Stormcloud's death, Aegon would never
fly again.

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:58.080
Now we come to the most epic, strongest, fiercest
and battle-hardened dragons:

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:02.040
Daemon's Ceraxes and again Aemond's Vhagar.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:05.470
The other dragon HBO teased in thier announcement
was Daemon's Caraxes.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:09.700
Caraxes was the dragon ridden by Prince Daemon
Targaryen during the Dance of the Dragons.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:15.810
A veteran of many battles, he was known as
the Blood Wyrm for his red scales.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:20.310
Caraxes was one of the older and larger dragons
during the Dance of the Dragons.

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:25.280
Daemon Targaryen rode Caraxes in his frequent
campaigns in the Stepstones.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:29.910
As a result Caraxes was not only one of the
larger dragons during the Dance, but the most

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:33.150
battle-hardened and experienced in war.

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:38.060
Indeed, only Vhagar had ever been ridden in
major wars before, during Aegon's Conquest

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:42.660
but while formidable, Vhagar had not been
used in combat in the years leading up to

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:45.250
the Dance, the way that Caraxes was.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:50.650
Opposing armies were known to often simply
flee or surrender when Caraxes approached.

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:55.040
When Rhaenyra captured King's Landing in a
surprise attack, Daemon rode Caraxes in the

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:58.190
assault while Rhaenyra rode Syrax.

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:03.740
Later in the war, Aegon II's younger brother
Aemond Targaryen resorted to a one-man war

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:07.710
riding Vhagar, burning out much of the Riverlands.

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:13.190
Daemon hunted him for a long time on Caraxes,
aided by other dragonriders and their dragons,

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:19.370
but eventually he returned alone to Harrenhal
waiting as a challenge for Aemond to arrive.

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:24.630
Caraxes was formidable but Vhagar was twice
his size, nearly as large as Balerion had

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:26.650
been during the War of Conquest.

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:31.380
Facing him alone was the only way for Daemon
to draw Vhagar out, however, as Aemond had

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:34.540
avoided ambushes by multiple other dragons.

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:40.580
Aemond arrived, exchanged his final challenges
to Daemon, then both took to the air on their

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:41.580
dragons.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:45.650
The resulting Battle Above the Gods Eye was
one of the most epic dragon-versus-dragon

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:50.330
fights of the entire civil war, as two of
the greatest living dragons fought in the

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:51.330
air.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:56.060
Their shrieks shattered every remaining window
in the castle and could be heard for miles

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:57.060
around.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:01.390
Their fire-breath filled the sky so that fishermen
in the lake thought that the whole sky was

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:02.440
aflame.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:07.320
In the end, Caraxes dove down from the sun
on Aemond's blind side (due to his missing

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:08.530
eye).

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:12.670
Caraxes slammed into Vhagar and they both
continued to fight in free fall.

00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:18.550
Vhagar tore out Caraxes's belly, and used
her massive jaws to rip one of his wing-arms

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:24.140
completely off - but Caraxes sank his teeth
into Vhagar's throat and maintained a death

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:25.140
grip.

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:30.580
As the two dragons grappled, Daemon rose from
his saddle and made a stunning mid-air leap

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:34.140
from his dragon to Aemond on Vhagar's back.

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:39.010
Wielding the Valyrian steel sword Dark Sister
(which had once been carried by Vhagar's previous

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:44.280
rider, Visenya Targaryen, Daemon thrust his
blade through Aemond's empty eye socket - the

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:49.690
force of his impact as he landed driving the
sword through the back of Aemond's head.

00:06:49.690 --> 00:06:52.650
Both dragons plummeted into Gods Eye below.

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:55.620
Both dragons and both dragonriders died.

00:06:55.620 --> 00:07:00.419
By the end of the Dance in 131 AC, only four
dragons remained alive:

00:07:00.419 --> 00:07:05.300
Sheepstealer, the Cannibal, and Silverwing,
who had been born years before the war,

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:08.240
and the dragon Morning, which had hatched
during the war.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:13.310
In other words, only one dragon who fought
during the Dance of the Dragons, Silverwing,

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:14.310
survived.

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:17.470
Dragon Morning was born after the war, while
the other two,

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:21.710
Sheepstealer and Cannibal were wild dragons
that lived on Dragonstone.

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:24.940
Sheepstealer was a wild male with a taste
for mutton.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:29.040
The smallfolk of Dragonstone named it for
a self-evident reason.

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:31.470
Sheepstealer's coloring was an ugly "mud brown".

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:35.820
He was not aggressive toward human unless
provoked, but could be vicious and ill-tempered.

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:37.770
He had a taste for mutton.

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:42.699
While he devoured an occasional sheep dog,
he never harmed a shepherd.

00:07:42.699 --> 00:07:48.650
The Cannibal got his name for practicing cannibalism,
feasting on dead dragons, newborn dragons,

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.240
and dragon eggs.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:54.130
He was one of three completely wild dragons
dwelling on Dragonstone.

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:58.030
The Cannibal was black as coal, with menacing
green eyes.

00:07:58.030 --> 00:08:01.540
He was the largest and oldest of the wild
dragons.

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:06.009
That's all that was left of 20 dragons that
Targaryens had had just a year and a half

00:08:06.009 --> 00:08:07.009
ago.

00:08:07.009 --> 00:08:08.590
And they would soon die as well.

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:11.449
Archmaester Marwyn, holds that the order of
maesters,

00:08:11.449 --> 00:08:17.240
with their secret goal to suppress magic,
was responsible for the extinction of dragons.

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:19.770
The word is that they poisoned the last of
the dragons.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:25.470
There were still many dragon eggs left after
the war, and at least one of those hatched.

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:31.270
The last dragon was a sick and misshapen thing,
and she died young, in 153 AC, during the

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:36.520
reign of King Aegon III Targaryen, which earned
him the nickname Dragonbane.

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:40.579
She had been a green female, small with withered
wings.

00:08:40.579 --> 00:08:44.190
Many futile attempts were made to revive dragons.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:49.589
Aegon III Targaryen, the Dragonbane, had nine
mages cross the narrow sea to use their magics

00:08:49.589 --> 00:08:52.730
in attempt to hatch remaining dragon eggs.

00:08:52.730 --> 00:08:58.360
The pious King Baelor I Targaryen attempted
to hatch his egg by praying over it.

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:03.600
Aegon IV Targaryen ordered pyromancers to
build seven mechanical "dragons" that shot

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.360
jets of wildfire.

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:09.430
Hundreds of men died in a failed attempt to
use them to invade Dorne.

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:14.650
The tragedy of Summerhall resulted from the
attempt of King Aegon V Targaryen to hatch

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:16.140
dragon eggs.

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:21.040
The Mad King pretended he was a dragon, using
wildfire to burn his enemies and believing

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:24.070
he would become a dragon after he dies.

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:27.230
None of these attempts brought dragons back
until Daenerys.

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:31.690
Ultimately, the reason Targaryens lost their
dragons and thus their power was the Dance

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:33.120
of the Dragons.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:38.160
So many dragons had died in the war that the
Targaryens couldn't maintain a stable breeding

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:41.670
population, and the few survivors became inbred
and sickly.

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:46.010
Fortunatlely, however, the key event of House
of the Dragon is the exact same event which

00:09:46.010 --> 00:09:51.570
led to their extinction - the Targaryen civil
war, the Dance of the Dragons and we'll get

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:53.070
to see them all on screen.

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:58.149
A lot of dragons, a lot of epic dragon battles,
all of that and more this Game of Thrones

00:09:58.149 --> 00:10:02.820
prequel series, House of the Dragons brings
in 2022 on HBO.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:07.100
Let me know your thoughts about everything:
the prequel, its characters, the mighty dragons

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:10.100
and their epic battles in the comment section
down below.

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:12.710
Thank you so much for watching, hope you enjoyed
this video and if you did make sure to give

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:14.959
it a big thumbs upand I hope to see you in
the next one, peace!

